#X obj 681 11 env.asr~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 286 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 An ASR (Attack / Sustain / Release) envelope generator
with three stages: attack (rise from 0 to 1) \, sustain (hold at the
sustain level while the gate is on) and release (fall back to 0 after
the gate is turned off). Unlike [env.adsr~] \, it has no decay stage
— the signal goes directly from attack to sustain. The envelope multiplies
the incoming audio signal by its current value.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Sustained notes — shaping the amplitude of a sound
that is held for as long as the key or gate is pressed \, with a smooth
attack and release and no artificial decay.;
#X text 250 294 • Pad and drone sounds — applying a slow attack and
long release to continuous textures \, so that they fade in and out
smoothly.;
